6795.stem:
A ball is thrown off the top of a building, and lands on the ground. The path of the ball can be modelled by the equation

$$h = 3.75 + 1.1x - 0.05x^2$$

where

\begin{itemize}
\item $h$ is the height above ground level in metres.
\item $x$ is the horizontal distance from the starting position in metres.
\end{itemize}

This equation is graphed below.

